FINAL: This report examines the state of Arctic sea ice and the viability of northern maritime shipping routes as observed throughout 2026. It covers the annual minimum ice extent, recent winter trends, the operational status of the Northwest Passage and Northern Sea Route, and the ongoing legal and environmental challenges affecting Arctic transit. The following sections detail these findings using data from satellite records, seasonal forecasts, and geopolitical analyses.

